cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "sem2txm"
abstract: >-
  An unpaired SEM-to-TXM image translator for cracked 316L stainless steel, built to
  test whether hand-drawn SEM crack labels can be carried across modalities to train
  a TXM crack detector. The result is negative and the repository is organised around
  establishing that precisely: measured against two registered SEM/TXM pairs, the
  translated image is a worse predictor of the real TXM than the raw SEM, and worse
  than a blurred copy of it. Four interventions (bounding pixel distortion, weakening
  the content constraint, removing the critic's access to intensity statistics, and
  matching the two modalities' physical scale) each fixed what they targeted and none
  changed the outcome. What does hold: hand-drawn SEM masks register on the
  translation exactly, and marked cracks retain their local contrast proportionally.
  Includes a validated cross-modality registration pipeline that refuses matches at
  the measured independence floor, and recovery of the SEM pixel size from the
  instrument's burned-in scale bar, cross-checked against FEI metadata to 0.07%.
  Reads its data from the sem-crack-detector and TXM_Crack_Detection_Pipeline
  repositories rather than shipping its own copy.
type: software
authors:
